    "case_id": "508",
    "case_summary": "A 25-year-old woman of Asian descent with no previous medical history presented after four days of fevers, fatigue, nausea, headaches, and malaise, along with an episode of vomiting. The patient continued to experience daily fevers exceeding 39°C over the next five days.\n\nPatient exhibited:- Temperature of 39.5°C- Heart rate of 130 beats/min- Blood pressure of 82/50 mm Hg (responded to fluids)- Tenderness in the left lower quadrant\n\nLaboratory Tests:- AST: 70 U/L (progressed to 383 U/L)- ALT: 55 U/L (progressed to 412 U/L)- LDH: 496 U/L- Ferritin: 773 ng/mL (increased to >7500)- Leukocyte count: 2000 cells/μL- Erythrocyte sedimentation rate: 41- Hemoglobin decreased to 10.3 g/dL- Thrombocytopenia presentImaging Studies:- CT of chest, abdomen, and pelvis  Image Description: Nonspecific inflammatory fat stranding and peritoneal thickening- CT angiogram  Image Description: Interval progression in intraperitoneal and extraperitoneal fluid and inflammatory changes with peritoneal thickeningBiopsy Results:- Peritoneal biopsy showed dense atypical lymphoid infiltrate involving adipose tissue lobules- Immunohistochemistry: Positive for CD3, CD8, CD7, CD43, CD5 (partial loss), TIA-1, granzyme B, CD2, and TCRβ F1; negative for TCRδ- Bone marrow biopsy suggested HLH- Elevated interleukin (IL)-2R alpha levels",
